ws of UX</span><span class=\"v2-nav-provenance\">Jon Yablonski</span></span><span class=\"v2-nav-pending\">5</span><span class=\"sw mini \" role=\"switch\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-checked=\"true\" aria-label=\"Laws of UX\"></span></a><button type=\"button\" class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary bn-btn-sm\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-nav-browse\">Browse Codebooks</button></nav></div><div class=\"drag-handle toc-drag-handle\" role=\"separator\" aria-orientation=\"vertical\" aria-valuenow=\"240\" aria-valuemin=\"200\" aria-valuemax=\"480\" aria-label=\"Resize table of contents\" tabindex=\"0\"></div></div>", "section": "<section data-testid=\"bn-codebook-v2\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><h1>Codebook</h1><div class=\"section-heading-action\"><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary bn-btn-lg\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-browse\">Browse Codebooks</button></div></div><div class=\"v2-layout\"><div class=\"v2-main\"><div data-testid=\"bn-v2-page\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><div class=\"pg-headmain\"><div class=\"pg-titlerow\"><div class=\"pg-titletext\"><div class=\"pg-title\">The Elements of User Experience</div><div class=\"pg-author\">Jesse James Garrett</div></div><div class=\"pg-titleaction\"><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-primary\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-install\">Install</button></div></div><div class=\"pg-stat\">18 tags · not installed</div><div class=\"pg-desc bn-lead-para\"><p class=\"bn-lead-claim\"><strong>Five planes of user experience, from abstract to concrete — strategy, scope, structure, skeleton, surface — each dependent on the plane below it, and each with two sides: the product as functionality and the product as information.</strong></p><p class=\"bn-lead-rest\">A framework for locating where in the design stack a finding lives: the objectives and needs behind the product, the features and content it includes, how its parts are arranged, how each screen is laid out, and what the senses meet.</p></div></div><div class=\"pg-side\"><div class=\"preview-author\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-author\"><div class=\"preview-author-name\">Jesse James Garrett</div><div class=\"preview-author-bio\">Co-founded the user experience consultancy Adaptive Path in 2001 (it became part of Capital One in 2014) and now coaches and advises design leaders. Coined the term \"Ajax\" (2005). The five-plane \"Elements\" diagram of March 2000 became \"The Elements of User Experience\" (New Riders, 2002; 2nd ed. \"User-Centered Design for the Web and Beyond\", 2010).</div><div class=\"preview-author-links\"><a href=\"https://jessejamesgarrett.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">jessejamesgarrett.com <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1em\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.25\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-external-link bn-icon bn-icon-external\" focusable=\"false\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" d=\"M15 3h6v6\"></path><path vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" d=\"M10 14 21 3\"></path><path vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" d=\"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6\"></path></svg></a><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0321683684\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Amazon US <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1em\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.25\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-external-link bn-icon bn-icon-external\" focusable=\"false\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" d=\"M15 3h6v6\"></path><path vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" d=\"M10 14 21 3\"></path><path vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" d=\"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6\"></path></svg></a><a href=\"https://www.amazon.co.uk/dp/0321683684\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Amazon UK <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=